skill: "goals-and-kpis"
sections[10]:
  - "\n"
  - "# goals-and-kpis\n\nThe **target-setting layer** — turn business outcomes into a measurable cascade with one **North Star\nper channel**, benchmark-set targets, and action thresholds. This skill **sets** the win conditions;\n**analytics-and-reporting measures** against them.\n\n"
  - "## The POV: goals, not wishes\n\"Grow our following,\" \"go viral,\" \"do better on Instagram\" are **wishes** — unmeasurable, unowned, and\ndisconnected from the business. Build a **cascade** instead: **business goal → SMART objective → KPI →\nsupporting metrics**, with **one North Star per channel** tied to its real job, a **target from your own\nbenchmark** (achievable yet ambitious), a **3–5 cap** for focus, and **thresholds that trigger action**.\nA KPI must be **controllable, non-vanity, and mapped to an outcome** — and a well-set one (a follower\ntarget paired with an engagement floor) **prevents gaming.**\n\n"
  - "## Read these first\n1. **brand-profile** — positioning/audience.\n2. **social-strategy** — the **business outcomes** every goal must ladder up to.\n\n"
  - "## The framework: NORTH\n(Depth: `references/the-north-framework.md`.)\n- **N — Name the business goal:** anchor every social goal to a real outcome (awareness/leads/sales/\n  retention); if it doesn't ladder up, cut it.\n- **O — One North Star per channel:** the single win-condition metric (awareness → reach; consideration\n  → CTR; conversion → CVR) + 1–2 supporting.\n- **R — Render it SMART:** Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound — a number + a deadline\n  + a method.\n- **T — Target from benchmarks:** set the number from your **baseline**/comparable benchmarks (no data →\n  a **learning goal** first); leading + lagging; only **controllable** KPIs.\n- **H — Hold to 3–5 + set triggers:** cap KPIs/objectives at 3–5; action thresholds (\"if X holds but Y\n  drops → do Z\"); review weekly/monthly/quarterly; hand to analytics-and-reporting.\n\n"
  - "## The reality (verify benchmarks quarterly)\nThe cascade, North-Star-per-channel, SMART, the funnel KPI map, the 3–5 rule, leading-vs-lagging +\nKPI-selection criteria, benchmark targets + thresholds, and review cadence:\n`references/goals-kpis-2026-reality.md`. North-star-by-channel table, goal→KPI cascades by business goal,\ntarget-setting + worked examples: `references/smart-goals-and-recipes.md`.\n\n"
  - "## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **Sets, doesn't measure** — measuring progress is **analytics-and-reporting** (WoopSocial post\n  analytics for the covered platforms; native dashboards otherwise). This skill defines targets,\n  North Stars, and thresholds, then hands off.\n- **Targets from real benchmarks** — **no fabricated baselines**; no data → a **learning goal** first;\n  comparable benchmarks are **provisional/flagged**.\n- **Controllable, non-vanity, outcome-mapped KPIs only.** Pair growth with a **quality guardrail** — a\n  well-set KPI **prevents gaming** (no follower-buying/pods).\n- **Realistic, not hype** — achievable yet ambitious; flag impossible asks. **Miss → pivot tactics first**,\n  don't move the goalposts or fudge numbers.\n  (Scope, distinctions + connections: `references/scope-and-connections.md`.)\n\n"
  - "## Distinct from its siblings (route correctly)\n**goals-and-kpis (this)** = SET targets/North Star/thresholds · **analytics-and-reporting** = MEASURE\nagainst them · **social-strategy** = the whole plan (this is its goals/KPI layer) · **experimentation** =\ntest tactics to move a KPI · **competitor-analysis** = benchmark context, not your own goals.\n\n"
  - "## Where this connects\nReads first: **brand-profile**, **social-strategy**. Benchmark inputs: **analytics-and-reporting**\n(baseline), **competitor-analysis** (relative), the **\\*-growth** skills (per-platform norms). Hands\ntargets to: **analytics-and-reporting** (measurement), **content-calendar**/**batch-content-plan**\n(cadence), **experimentation** (tests), **campaign-and-launch-planning** (campaign KPIs). Per-channel\nNorth Stars draw on the per-platform growth skills. No publishing/tool surface — a planning skill.\n\n"
  - "## Definition of done\nA cascade per goal (business outcome → SMART objective with number+deadline+method → one North Star per\nchannel + 1–2 supporting); targets set from real baselines/benchmarks (or a learning goal if none),\nachievable yet ambitious, with a quality guardrail; capped at 3–5 with action thresholds and a weekly/\nmonthly/quarterly review cadence; controllable, non-vanity, outcome-mapped KPIs; handed to\nanalytics-and-reporting to measure; nothing fabricated, correctly distinguished from analytics-and-reporting,\nsocial-strategy, and experimentation.\n"
